<div class="document">
<p>Every physical component SHALL expose a dynamic ODE model.</p>
<p>Each component SHALL explicitly define: state vector, state units, initial conditions,
input variables, output variables, governing differential equations, algebraic constitutive
relations, physical parameters, boundary conditions, conservation residuals, numerical
constraints, and associated StrictDoc requirement IDs.</p>
<p>Every component SHALL provide a rhs() method returning state derivatives.</p>
<p>The generic mathematical representation SHALL be:</p>
<blockquote>
dx/dt = f(t, x, inputs, parameters)</blockquote>
<p>Where required:</p>
<blockquote>
0 = g(t, x, algebraic_variables, inputs, parameters)</blockquote>
<p>Algebraic variables SHALL be solved consistently during RHS evaluation or through a
supported DAE backend.</p>
<p>An artificial time constant SHALL NOT be introduced solely to make an instantaneous
physical relation appear dynamic.</p>
<p>Passive structures, such as current collectors, SHALL possess actual dynamic states
where justified, such as temperature. Their instantaneous electrical resistance SHALL
remain an algebraic relation.</p>
</div>
